# Changelog

## [Unreleased]
- ATS/Modern headers: conditional `|` separator — fields `%`-commented out in `config/personal.tex` automatically lose their separator, no `Undefined control sequence`.
- Banner links split into `Url` (href) vs `Label` (display); old files using `\cvGithub` etc. still compile via the legacy bridge.
- `\cvLink{bare-url}{label}` helper + multi-link examples (`repo \cvSep demo`) in `sections/en|id/projects.tex`, verified clickable (6 link annots).
- Watch mode: job `cv-<variant>-<lang>`, target validation, `--all --watch` explicitly rejected.
- Docs: Prerequisites section in README (Arch, Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora, macOS,
  Windows) + explicit `pdftotext`/`pdfinfo` check during `--check-ats`.
- Shell completions for `compile.sh` (zsh + bash): installer script, conflict-aware
  suggestions, optional direnv support. `--academic` deliberately not suggested
  until `templates/academic/` exists.

## [0.1.0] — 2026-09-08
- Initial scaffold: dual-mode (ats/modern) x dual-lang (ID/EN), 4 PDF outputs.
- `config/order.tex` for section order/on-off, folder-per-variant templates.
- `compile.sh` port from template-ta + `--check-ats` validation.
- Minimal-modular sections: summary, education, experience, projects, skills (+ optional certifications, organizations).
